    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d235">

                <pb facs="0362" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.51/294: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Thurston</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-05-23T14:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23, 1919, 2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received May 25, 245
                            a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>See despatch number 506 dated April 30, 1918, enclosure number 1.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d235-f1"/></p>
                <p>A commission has just been appointed for the purpose of devising means whereby a
                    national bank may be established.</p>
                <p>I am reliably informed that the proposed issue of 60,000,000 pesos has been
                    canceled and that only 10,000,000 will be given the Banco Americano.</p>
                <p>In the opinion of bankers this renewal of interest in the national bank indicates
                    tendency in favor of a foreign loan since it is not felt the necessary capital
                    could be commanded locally for its establishment.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
